   This example demonstrates how to use QuantLib to perform a discounted cash flow (DCF) valuation.

   ## Overview

   The example calculates the net present value (NPV) of a series of fixed cash flows (like a bond) using a flat yield curve. It also calculates duration and convexity, and shows the sensitivity to a parallel shift in the yield curve.

